    "result_text": "The build succeeds \u2014 the single acceptance test passes, and the audit log confirms the new identity end to end: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, with sequence numbers dropped, and every value derived from it moved along with it. I kept each concern in its own small unit and reused the existing SHA-256 code rather than copying it.\n\n**New util classes** (single-responsibility, in the `util` package alongside `Luhn`, `CityRegion`, etc.):\n- `Sha256` \u2014 shared lower-case hex SHA-256. Extracted from the private copy inside `Households`, which now reuses it (no duplicated hashing).\n- `OwnerRegion` \u2014 the region derivation (postcode-first via `PostcodeRange.regionOf`, then the city table, else `UNKNOWN`). This is the logic that previously lived inline in the mapper's `locality()`.\n- `CustomerCode` \u2014 the identity format: `of(region, telephone, lastName)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex of `SHA-256(telephone + lastName)`), and `regionOf(code)` reads the REGION segment back.\n\n**Behaviour moves onto the new identity:**\n- `AssignCustomerCode` now builds `OwnerRegion.of(owner)` + hash, using the already-normalized E.164 telephone. It no longer needs the repository or per-city count.\n- **Membership number** (`AssignMembershipNumber`) and **check digit** (`OwnerMapper.checkDigit` via `Luhn`) read `customerCode` unchanged, so they automatically reflect the new code; `Luhn` correctly ignores the hex letters.\n- **Audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) logs the new `customerCode` unchanged.\n- **Locality** (`OwnerMapper.locality`) now reads the REGION segment out of the customerCode (`CustomerCode.regionOf`), so there is one region concept sourced from the identity rather than a parallel derivation.\n\n**Docs kept in sync:** Javadoc on the touched classes, `Cities` (no longer feeds a code sequence), the `owners.POST.yml` step comment, and the `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`.\n\nOne deliberate design point worth flagging: I made the REGION reuse the existing postcode-then-city fallback (`OwnerRegion`) so a known city without a postcode keeps its old region value, and locality reads that same value back off the code \u2014 a single source of truth. The spec's \"derived from the postcode\" is honoured for the primary path (the test's postcode `2000` \u2192 `NSW`), and the fallback only matters when no postcode resolves.",
